// Personal wishes of villagers (#2601). Each row is a template the server coins a concrete wish from, per player and
// place: "deliver" = bring me (the items are handed over), "show" = show me (the player keeps them), "scan" = check on
// the animals (scanner). "requires" keeps a wish the world cannot grant from ever being asked (flora_drop | trees |
// mycelium | creatures | ""); a template of tier T comes up once T-1 wishes of that lane were fulfilled. "jobs" limits
// who may wish it ("" = a plain settler, gardener, craftsman, innkeeper; empty list = everyone). "reason" is an English
// hint for the AI re-wording only. Texts: wish.<key>.ask / wish.<key>.thanks in data/locales (en + de mandatory).
